 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Convert an action to subject or object",
   "texto": [
    "**-는 것** permite hablar de una acción como «hacer…» o «el hecho de…»: 수영하다 → **수영하는 것** (nadar), 여행하다 → **여행하는 것** (viajar), 요리하다 → **요리하는 것** (cocinar). When carrying a particle, **것** is usually contracted: **수영하는 걸 좋아해요** is the spoken form of **수영하는 것을 좋아해요**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Talk about tastes",
   "texto": [
    "With **좋아하다/싫어하다** the nomineed action usually carries the **을/를** object: **여행하는 것을 좋아해요** (I like to travel), **수영하는 것을 싫어해요** (I don't like to swim). With **좋다/싫다**, it is common to mark it as a theme with **은/는**: **수영하는 것은 싫어요**. They are related constructions, but the particles and the preaching are not just interchangeable."
   ]
  },
